x86_64-windows  four guards cxx1 writes and clang does not: ?Identity@?$Consts@UTag1@@@@2UR@@B$guard and its three neighbours. A template's static member is defined in every translation unit that instantiates it, and something has to keep the second copy from building it again - clang puts each one's construction in its own COMDAT function, ??__E...@@YAXXZ, so the linker keeps one; cxx1 builds everything in the one init function and guards each with a weak flag beside the object, which is the shape clang itself uses on the Itanium targets (_ZGVN6ConstsI4Tag1E8IdentityE, where the two agree). One guard per object, nothing links against it
